    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="0762" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/318</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 508</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-02">July 2, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received July 3.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to the plan to
                    settle the remainder of the public works debt, I have the honor to report that,
                    according to today’s press, the House of Representatives met yesterday and
                    adjourned until July 18. It is obvious, therefore, that the House of
                    Representatives, at least, will give no further consideration to either of the
                    bills to settle the public works debt until after that date.</p>
                <p>The Senate, of course, has not met since it received its powers to legislate from
                    the Constituent Assembly, and there is no reason to believe that it intends to
                    meet until sometime after presidential elections on July 14.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George S.
                    Messersmith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
